(7691606, 1260487, 30214, '<td valign="top"><img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=86447" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">Lydia</a>, thank you for the compliment on my lighting skills!   I will let you in on a secret, my daughter is a theatrical <a href="//www.mashald.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">lighting designer</a>, I must have acquired my skills from her through some kind of reverse genetics :).<br/> <br/><img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21_F.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=124815" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">mariuca</a> yes, that bush on the way to my front door bugged me as well, but I could not find a better spot for this photo without making a much greater effort of shooting "on location". Of course, an urban environment (New York brownstone, preferably :)) would have been a lot better, but you play with what you got...<br/> <br/><img border="0" src="https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif" xalt="'' . substr(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', strrpos(''https://www.dpchallenge.com/images/user_icon/21.gif'', ''/'') + 1) . ''"/> <a href="https://www.dpchallenge.com/profile.php?USER_ID=143116" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">bsluijk</a> yes indeed it would''ve been a much nicer explanation, although a little hard to believe in, since 1 and 10 are pretty far away on the range of scores to accidentally click on one instead of another :)<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2021-04-12 15:29:41.</i></td>', ' Lydia, thank you for the compliment on my lighting skills!   I will let you in on a secret, my daughter is a theatrical lighting designer, I must have acquired my skills from her through some kind of reverse genetics :).  mariuca yes, that bush on the way to my front door bugged me as well, but I could not find a better spot for this photo without making a much greater effort of shooting "on location". Of course, an urban environment (New York brownstone, preferably :)) would have been a lot better, but you play with what you got...  bsluijk yes indeed it would''ve been a much nicer explanation, although a little hard to believe in, since 1 and 10 are pretty far away on the range of scores to accidentally click on one instead of another :)', '2021-04-12 15:05:34.000000', '2021-04-12 16:29:41.000000', 0),
