</i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>MANY CONGRATS ON THE BLUE LEV .. <br/>it satisfied the challenge perfectly .. <br/>and thankyou so much for the backstory and for your replies ... <br/>i love reading what went on behind the scenes .. :)</td>', 'Originally posted by LevT:  Lydia, thank you for the compliment on my lighting skills!   I will let you in on a secret, my daughter is a theatrical lighting designer, I must have acquired my skills from her through some kind of reverse genetics :).  mariuca yes, that bush on the way to my front door bugged me as well, but I could not find a better spot for this photo without making a much greater effort of shooting "on location". Of course, an urban environment (New York brownstone, preferably :)) would have been a lot better, but you play with what you got...  bsluijk yes indeed it would''ve been a much nicer explanation, although a little hard to believe in, since 1 and 10 are pretty far away on the range of scores to accidentally click on one instead of another :)   MANY CONGRATS ON THE BLUE LEV .. it satisfied the challenge perfectly .. and thankyou so much for the backstory and for your replies ... i love reading what went on behind the scenes .. :)', '2021-04-16 20:52:07.000000', NULL, 0),
